From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Leave the sounds a desktop makes on its own account where they are

What is playing when a cast begins is moved onto it, which is what somebody
casting wants for a film or a podcast. It is not what they want for the short
sounds a desktop makes about itself: a message arriving, a device being
plugged in, a warning, something being read aloud. Those are answers to what
is happening at this machine. Sent to a television, they are how a room full
of people learns that somebody has had an email.

A desktop says what a sound is for, so those are left where they were, along
with anything marked as a call, which belongs to whoever is wearing the
headset rather than to the room.

Everything else moves as before. A sound that says nothing about itself is
treated as something to send, since that is what most things playing are.

diff -ruN a/src/nd-pulseaudio.c b/src/nd-pulseaudio.c
--- a/src/nd-pulseaudio.c
+++ b/src/nd-pulseaudio.c
@@ -162,11 +162,30 @@
   NdPulseaudio *self = ND_PULSEAUDIO (userdata);
 
   g_autofree gchar *sink_name = NULL;
+  const char *role;
   pa_operation *operation;
 
   if (eol || info == NULL)
     return;
 
+  /* Not everything playing is something to send. A desktop names what a
+   * sound is for, and the short ones it makes on its own account - a message
+   * arriving, a device being plugged in, a warning, something read aloud -
+   * are answers to what is happening at this machine, not part of what is
+   * being shown on a television. Sending them is how a room full of people
+   * learns that somebody has had an email. They stay where they were, and so
+   * does anything a desktop marks as a call, which belongs to whoever is
+   * wearing the headset rather than to the room. */
+  role = pa_proplist_gets (info->proplist, PA_PROP_MEDIA_ROLE);
+  if (role != NULL &&
+      (g_str_equal (role, "event") ||
+       g_str_equal (role, "a11y") ||
+       g_str_equal (role, "phone")))
+    {
+      g_debug ("NdPulseaudio: Leaving %s (%s) where it is", info->name, role);
+      return;
+    }
+
   sink_name = g_strdup_printf (ND_PA_SINK "_%.8s", self->uuid);
 
   g_debug ("NdPulseaudio: Moving what is playing (%u) to %s", info->index, sink_name);
